  "findings": "A dependency chain had stalled: its root job was dead-lettered after exhausting three retries, holding a waiting descendant behind it, while the upstream parent had completed normally. Because dead_letter is terminal and the resolver only promotes a child once every parent has completed, the chain could not drain on its own. Replaying the root returned replayed=1 with scheduled=0, and a follow-up read showed the chain fully drained.\n",
  "recommendation": "Read the root's error_message to find why it exhausted its retries — the replay cleared the symptom, not the cause, and a chain that dead-letters again will stall the same way. If the failure is an external dependency, consider whether the job's retry budget is sized for it.\n",
